From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: apklayer <apklayer@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] ShadowKeyCharacterMap: no character under Ctrl/Alt/Meta

apklayer patch (docs/PATCHES.md "Proxied IME and clipboard"): AOSP KeyCharacterMap.matchesMetaState requires exact Ctrl/Alt/Meta
matches; without this Ctrl+V typed 'v' before Android shortcuts ran. Covered by tests/vm/input.sh.

Against external/robolectric 87aa52b08 (REVISION). Applied by scripts/build-runtime-overlay.sh onto the staged
upstream sources (<native>/aosp/robolectric-src); the result is compiled into native-runtime.jar ahead of Robolectric_all.jar.
---
diff --git a/shadows/framework/src/main/java/org/robolectric/shadows/ShadowKeyCharacterMap.java b/shadows/framework/src/main/java/org/robolectric/shadows/ShadowKeyCharacterMap.java
--- a/shadows/framework/src/main/java/org/robolectric/shadows/ShadowKeyCharacterMap.java
+++ b/shadows/framework/src/main/java/org/robolectric/shadows/ShadowKeyCharacterMap.java
@@ -219,6 +219,11 @@
 
   @Implementation
   protected static char nativeGetCharacter(long ptr, int keyCode, int metaState) {
+    // apklayer patch: AOSP KeyCharacterMap.matchesMetaState requires exact
+    // Ctrl/Alt/Meta matches. Otherwise Ctrl+V types 'v' before shortcuts run.
+    if ((metaState & (KeyEvent.META_CTRL_MASK | KeyEvent.META_ALT_MASK | KeyEvent.META_META_MASK)) != 0) {
+      return 0;
+    }
     boolean metaShiftOn = (metaState & KeyEvent.META_SHIFT_ON) != 0;
     Character character = KEY_CODE_TO_CHAR.get(keyCode);
     if (character == null) {
